  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Kansas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Kansas, the case concerns whether Kansas' civil\u2011commitment statute requires proof that a sexually violent predator cannot control his behavior, in addition to the traditional requisites of mental illness and dangerousness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "State",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The State argues that the statute should be limited to volitional impairments and that emotional impairments are not valid under the law."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court has previously held in *Hendricks* that inability to control behavior was the appropriate level of mental illness for civil commitment."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Kansas",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Kansas, kansas asserts that the Kansas Supreme Court misread *Hendricks* by requiring a showing that a potentially sexually violent predator cannot control his behavior, adding to the two requisites of mental illness and dangerousness."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Kansas (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "State",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The State contends that the legislature did not define \"mental abnormality,\" but that the term includes both emotional and volitional impairments, and argues that only volitional impairments should be permissible under the statute."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Donham",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Mr. Donham argued that the Kansas act is constitutional because it does not rely solely on dangerousness, referencing *Foucha v. Louisiana*, and that the additional element distinguishes cases like *Hendricks*."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Donham",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "1665b5fc5b3512251c1de816ba66626b3ee00ccaedae5fe2e5c07831187413f3",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-1665b5fc5b35-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 38,
                "start": 38
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Donham, mr. Donham also noted that *Hendricks* admitted an inability to control behavior, suggesting that such admission is central to the statutory analysis."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "State (Respondent)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    }
